{
 "constants": {
  "rule": "Rule RU. (1) Before every seed step (seed or reseed) at voxel v, take the voxels accepted so far in the run (seed test passed or fitted in the BFS, not rejected since: state FITTED) and keep the 8 nearest to v by centre distance (ties by voxel index; any distance; fewer if fewer exist; none: go to (4)). (2) Take the strict cost of each one's orientation at v (one evaluation each). From the lowest-cost one (ties: nearer first), run one CMA local optimization: first step 0.5 degree, 200 evaluations, a fresh default_rng(0). If the end's hit ratio (one overlap evaluation, not counted, as in the library) is 0.95 or more, the end is the seed result. Then there is no indexing and no seed step, and the BFS goes on as after a passing seed step. (3) Else, run the same fit from the lowest-cost start more than 0.5 degree from the first (if any), with the same acceptance. (4) Else the PXF seed step runs unchanged. All try evaluations count as the seed's. Nothing else changes. No truth, no threshold read from data after this freeze, nothing crystal-specific (misorientation under the sample's symmetry group; any group works). Script layer only: a wrapper of the seed step of the pick that the library's BFSReconstruction._index_seed calls, on top of PXF's.",
